  "subject": "Discoloured Dermacalm cream caused a burning rash",
  "sender": "Priya Raman <priya.raman@mailbox.example>",
  "recipient": "Pharmacovigilance Intake <pv-intake@clinevo-demo.example>",
  "sent_at": "2026-03-17T09:00:00Z",
  "received_at": "2026-09-08T03:35:33.368686Z",
  "body_text": "Hello,\n\nI bought a tube of Dermacalm cream last month, batch number DC-4471-B. When I opened it the cream was brown rather than white and smelled strongly of chemicals. The seal under the cap was already broken.\n\nI used it anyway on my forearm and within an hour I had a burning sensation and the skin blistered. I am 33 years old. I saw my pharmacist who told me to stop using it and report it. The blisters are healing now.\n\nI have photographs of the tube and my arm if those are useful.\n\nPriya Raman, Leeds, UK",
